<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <%- include('partials/seo-head') %>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <%- themeCSS %>
  <style>
    .tutorial-shell { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 70px 24px 90px; }
    .tutorial-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .92fr 1.08fr; gap: 28px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 38px; }
    .tutorial-hero h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); line-height: .92; margin: 0 0 18px; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
    .tutorial-hero p { color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 680px; }
    .tutorial-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 26px; }
    .tutorial-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 20px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
    .tutorial-button.primary { background: var(--accent); color: #07110d; border-color: transparent; }
    .tutorial-player { border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); border-radius: 28px; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(20,27,42,.96), rgba(8,12,20,.98)); box-shadow: 0 26px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.34); overflow: hidden; }
    .player-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .82rem; }
    .player-dots { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
    .player-dot { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: rgba(255,255,255,.25); }
    .player-screen { min-height: 330px; padding: 0; display: block; position: relative; overflow: hidden; background:#05070a; }
    .tutorial-video-img { display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; }
    .player-screen:before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: -35%; background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, rgba(0,232,123,.16), transparent 35%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 50%, rgba(100,150,255,.18), transparent 32%); animation: slowPan 9s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
    .screen-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
    .screen-step { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 800; font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .screen-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1; margin: 12px 0; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
    .screen-caption { color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    .screen-narration { position: relative; z-index: 1; padding: 16px; border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(4,7,12,.72); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); color: #eef6f1; line-height: 1.55; }
    .tutorial-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 24px; }
    .tutorial-card { border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); border-radius: 22px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.045); padding: 20px; }
    .tutorial-card strong { display: block; color: var(--accent); font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .tutorial-card h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
    .tutorial-card p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; font-size: .95rem; }
    .tutorial-section { margin-top: 54px; }
    .tutorial-section h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); margin: 0 0 16px; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
    .demo-credentials { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-top: 18px; }
    .credential-box { border: 1px solid rgba(0,232,123,.18); border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(0,232,123,.07); padding: 16px; }
    .credential-box span { display: block; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: .74rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .12em; margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .credential-box code { color: #fff; font: 700 1rem var(--font-display); word-break: break-word; }
    .transcript { display: grid; gap: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
    .transcript details { border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.04); padding: 14px 16px; }
    .transcript summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; color: var(--fg); }
    .transcript p { color: var(--fg-muted); margin: 10px 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }
    .checklist { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .check-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: start; padding: 16px; border-radius: 18px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); background: rgba(255,255,255,.04); }
    .check-mark { width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 12px; display: grid; place-items: center; background: rgba(0,232,123,.12); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 900; }
    .check-item b { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .check-item span { color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
    .app-map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 18px; }
    .app-card { border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); border-radius: 20px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.04); padding: 18px; }
    .app-card strong { display: block; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .app-card p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; font-size: .94rem; }
    @keyframes slowPan { from { transform: translate3d(-1%, -1%, 0) scale(1); } to { transform: translate3d(1%, 1%, 0) scale(1.05); } }
    @media (max-width: 920px) {
      .tutorial-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .tutorial-grid, .app-map { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .tutorial-shell { padding: 46px 16px 70px; }
      .tutorial-grid, .app-map, .demo-credentials { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .player-screen { min-height: auto; padding: 0; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>
  <main class="tutorial-shell">
    <section class="tutorial-hero">
      <div>
        <h1>Your Autovyne signup walkthrough.</h1>
        <p>This quick overview shows the full path a new customer follows: sign up, choose payment, get activated, and use the client portal without needing to open every technical app behind the scenes.</p>
        <div class="tutorial-actions">
          <a class="tutorial-button primary" href="/signup">Start Signup</a>
          <a class="tutorial-button" href="/demo">Try ROI + Live Demo</a>
          <a class="tutorial-button" href="/portal">Open Client Portal</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tutorial-player" aria-label="Autovyne signup video overview">
        <div class="player-top">
          <div class="player-dots"><span class="player-dot"></span><span class="player-dot"></span><span class="player-dot"></span></div>
          <span>Autovyne Signup-to-Portal Walkthrough</span>
        </div>
        <div class="player-screen">
          <img class="tutorial-video-img" src="/media/autovyne-demo-walkthrough.gif" alt="Animated Autovyne walkthrough showing signup, payment, portal activation, dashboard usage, action center, and demo login details.">
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tutorial-grid" aria-label="Step-by-step signup overview">
      <article class="tutorial-card">
        <strong>Step 01</strong>
        <h2>Start Signup</h2>
        <p>Choose a monthly plan, enter business details, create a portal password, and choose whether SMS consent applies.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tutorial-card">
        <strong>Step 02</strong>
        <h2>Pay or Review</h2>
        <p>Automatic billing goes through Stripe. Manual billing creates a review item before activation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tutorial-card">
        <strong>Step 03</strong>
        <h2>Activate Account</h2>
        <p>After payment or approval, the account opens with email plus the portal password or access code.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tutorial-card">
        <strong>Step 04</strong>
        <h2>Manage Portal</h2>
        <p>Customers can see services, activity, recovered value, onboarding progress, and safe control requests.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="tutorial-section">
      <h2>Demo account for the video</h2>
      <p class="screen-caption">Use this test account when recording sales walkthroughs, onboarding videos, or customer demos. It is intentionally separate from real customer data.</p>
      <div class="demo-credentials">
        <div class="credential-box"><span>Email</span><code>demo@autovyne.com</code></div>
        <div class="credential-box"><span>Access Code</span><code>AutovyneDemo2026!</code></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tutorial-section">
      <h2>What the apps do behind the scenes</h2>
      <p class="screen-caption">Customers do not need to download or learn all these tools. Autovyne connects them in the background and shows the plain-English status inside the client portal.</p>
      <div class="app-map">
        <article class="app-card"><strong>OpenAI</strong><p>Summarizes leads, explains account activity, powers the portal helper, and supports admin review without sending messages by itself.</p></article>
        <article class="app-card"><strong>Twilio</strong><p>Handles approved SMS workflows, STOP/HELP replies, and phone-number messaging rules when consent records allow it.</p></article>
        <article class="app-card"><strong>HubSpot</strong><p>Stores contacts and lead status so follow-up is organized instead of scattered across notes and inboxes.</p></article>
        <article class="app-card"><strong>n8n</strong><p>Moves events between Autovyne, CRM, SMS, alerts, and onboarding workflows after the right checks pass.</p></article>
        <article class="app-card"><strong>Stripe</strong><p>Runs secure monthly subscription checkout and lets automatic-billing customers manage payment settings.</p></article>
        <article class="app-card"><strong>Supabase</strong><p>Stores portal accounts, consent proof, questions, activity, metrics, and compliance records.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tutorial-section">
      <h2>What customers see after signup</h2>
      <div class="checklist">
        <div class="check-item">
          <div class="check-mark">1</div>
          <div><b>Portal status</b><span>Customers can see whether their AI calling, SMS, CRM, and workflow automation services are pending, connected, or live.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <div class="check-mark">2</div>
          <div><b>Onboarding progress</b><span>The account shows what Autovyne is setting up next, so new users are not left guessing after payment.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <div class="check-mark">3</div>
          <div><b>Simple AI help</b><span>The customer assistant explains portal items, service status, and next steps without giving admin-only control.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <div class="check-mark">4</div>
          <div><b>Industry-aware setup</b><span>The AI follows the same Autovyne workflow for every account, then adjusts wording and priorities for the customer industry.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tutorial-section">
      <h2>Narration transcript</h2>
      <div class="transcript">
        <details open><summary>1. Signup</summary><p>First, the owner starts signup. They choose a plan, billing method, and enter the basic business details Autovyne needs for onboarding.</p></details>
        <details><summary>2. Payment</summary><p>Next, payment decides the activation path. Stripe subscriptions can activate automatically after checkout, while manual billing stays under Autovyne review.</p></details>
        <details><summary>3. Activation</summary><p>Once the account is approved, the client portal becomes the simple home base for status, setup progress, and customer support.</p></details>
        <details><summary>4. Portal Usage</summary><p>Inside the portal, the customer does not need HubSpot, Twilio, n8n, or Stripe tabs. They see the plain-English version of what is happening.</p></details>
        <details><summary>5. Control Requests</summary><p>If a customer wants to block a caller, pause follow-up, or request review, they use Action Center. Autovyne reviews requests before changing outreach.</p></details>
        <details><summary>6. Demo Login</summary><p>For sales demos, use the demo account. It shows a live-style portal without exposing real customer data.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
